    narr:narration """This narrative holds the case that [the hero video is a human moment, not a screen recording](narr:Expr_1RealFreyaPodcastSalesMotion20260323_15), grounded in the rule [don't make people read text in a video](narr:Expr_1RealFreyaPodcastSalesMotion20260323_14). The principle is operationalized as [a five-beat format running from real call footage to the expert's reaction](narr:Expr_1RealFreyaPodcastSalesMotion20260323_16), with a production path [assembled from existing Tess call footage or a new short recording](narr:Expr_1RealFreyaPodcastSalesMotion20260323_17). The underlying claim is that [the human moment sells, not the text](narr:Expr_1RealFreyaPodcastSalesMotion20260323_18), and the mechanism that makes the cited output trustworthy is [the `, aswritten` mode switch telling the AI to use real sources](narr:Expr_1RealFreyaPodcastSalesMotion20260323_20), so that [the viewer learns what this means by seeing the output change](narr:Expr_1RealFreyaPodcastSalesMotion20260323_21). A relayed account records [Freya's reaction confirming the human moment sells better than any screen recording](narr:Expr_1RealFreyaPodcastSalesMotion20260323_8).""" ;
    narr:covers <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_1RealFreyaPodcastSalesMotion20260323_14> ;
    narr:covers <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_1RealFreyaPodcastSalesMotion20260323_15> ;
